                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/417: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-16T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 16,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>234. Your 485, October 16, 1 p.m. Action proposed by you has approval of
                    Department which is of the opinion that the record should be clear on the
                    subject of taxes such as those proposed at Canton and in Shantung.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
